WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.570
In illness or grief, many Christians turn
to Bible passages they know by heart.

2
00:00:05.620 --> 00:00:08.900
Every Sunday, churches
read set passages aloud,

3
00:00:08.950 --> 00:00:11.360
and preachers explain what they mean.

4
00:00:11.410 --> 00:00:15.370
Yet the newest of its books was
written nearly 2,000 years ago,

5
00:00:15.420 --> 00:00:17.390
in a very different world.

6
00:00:17.440 --> 00:00:22.150
So how do Christians get advice for
life today from a book that old?

7
00:00:22.200 --> 00:00:26.050
In this mission, you'll see how
Christians use the Bible in worship,

8
00:00:26.100 --> 00:00:29.050
in prayer and in everyday choices.

9
00:00:29.100 --> 00:00:31.540
Then you'll line up ways
of reading the Bible,

10
00:00:31.590 --> 00:00:34.550
from plain sense to a human document.

11
00:00:34.600 --> 00:00:39.270
Your mission: find out how Christians
draw advice for today from a book finished

12
00:00:39.320 --> 00:00:41.330
nearly 2,000 years ago.
